    "lawCode": "Amd §1-d, rel §§1-u & 1-v to be §§1-v & 1-w, add §1-u, Leg L",
    "lawSection": "Legislative Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S426\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the legislative law, in relation to authorizing the\ncommission on ethics and lobbying in government to provide a training\ncourse concerning anti-sexual harassment training for lobbyists and\nrequiring lobbyists to complete the course annually\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require anti-sexual harassment training for lobbyists appearing\nbefore members of the legislature.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Directs the Commission on Ethics and Lobbying in Government\nto develop an anti-sexual harassment training curriculum required for\nregistered lobbyists. The curriculum shall include materials specific to\nthe lobbying and advocacy industry. Lobbyists who have not completed the\ntraining by the required date will be prohibited from engaging in lobby-\ning activities.\n\nSection 2: Requires registered lobbyists to complete the anti-sexual\nharassment training course annually.\n\nSection 3: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Department of Labor has long recognized the need for anti-harassment\ntraining to help prevent hostile work environments.  Annual training to\nprevent sexual harassment is mandated for all legislators and legisla-\ntive staff.\n\nLobbyists frequently work in close proximity to legislators, legislative\nstaff, and government officials, and they must register with the state\nin order to conduct business before the New York State government. As a\ncondition of their registration, lobbyists should undergo annual anti-\nsexual harassment training, similar to that required of the Legislature,\nto ensure they uphold the standards expected in the NYS government.\nThis simple requirement for lobbyists will help protect legislators,\nlegislative employees, and lobbyists alike from harassment and miscon-\nduct.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n05/13/24 REPORTED AND COMMITTED TO FINANCE\n\n06/01/23 PASSED SENATE; REFERRED TO GOVERNMENTAL OPERATIONS\n\n2022: THIRD READING\n\n2021: PASSED SENATE\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to individuals\nregistered as lobbyists on and after January 1, 2026.\n",
